REGENT OF EAST LUWU
SOUTH SULAWESI PROVINCE
COPY
REGIONAL REGULATION OF EAST LUWU REGENCY
NUMBER 4 YEAR 2021
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AGAINST VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF EAST LUWU,
Considering : a. that in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women to be free from torture and treatment that degrades human dignity and to improve the quality of life, women have the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, provides affirmation of the need for protection and provision of a sense of security to women;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women Against Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
3. Law Number 7 Year 2003 concerning the Establishment of East Luwu Regency and North Mamuju Regency in South Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 27, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4270);
4. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 44 Year 2008 concerning Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 181, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4928);
6. Law Number 16 Year 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5248);
7. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 11 Year 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);
8. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 Year 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 Year 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 12 Year 2017 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Classification of Branch Offices and Regional Technical Implementation Units (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2017 Number 451);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 4 Year 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2018 Number 532);
13. Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 8 Year 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Year 2016 Number 8) as amended by Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 5 Year 2020 concerning Amendment to Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 8 Year 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Year 2020 Number 5, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Number 124).
With Mutual Approval

text:
BAB III
HAK PEREMPUAN KORBAN KEKERASAN
Pasal 4
Perempuan korban kekerasan berhak :
a. dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia;
b. mendapatkan informasi perlindungan perempuan;
c. memperoleh rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi sosial;
d. memperoleh pemulihan kesehatan fisik, psikologis maupun seksual  sesuai penderitaan yang dialami korban kekerasan;
e. memperoleh pemberdayaan dan pendampingan hukum; dan f. pelayanan bimbingan rohani.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF FEMALE VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Female victims of violence have the right to:
a. have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
b. obtain information on the protection of women;
c. obtain rehabilitation and social reintegration;
d. obtain physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
e. obtain empowerment and legal assistance; and f. receive spiritual guidance services.

text:
Pasal 7
(1) Dalam perlindungan perempuan dilakukan pencegahan kekerasan. (2) Pencegahan sebagaimana ayat (1) dilaksanakan dengan cara: a. mensosialisasikan peraturan perundang-undangan;
b. memberikan edukasi bahaya kekerasan terhadap perempuan; c. melakukan seminar/lokakarya atau sejenisnya;
d. menjalin kerja sama dengan instansi pemerintah atau lembaga non pemerintah dalam upaya pencegahan kekerasan; dan
e. membentuk sistem pencegahan, pemetaan lokasi atau wilayah rawan  terjadinya kekerasan.
(3) Pencegahan kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dapat berkoordinasi dengan lembaga lain.

translated_text:
Article 7
(1) In the protection of women, prevention of violence is carried out. (2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by means of: a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. providing education on the dangers of violence against women; c. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
d. establishing cooperation with government agencies or non-governmental institutions in efforts to prevent violence; and
e. establishing a prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to violence.
(3) Prevention of violence as referred to in paragraph (2) may coordinate with other institutions.

text:
Pasal 8
Pelayanan terhadap korban kekerasan dilaksanakan berdasarkan prinsip :  a. tidak dipungut biaya;
b. cepat;
c. aman dan nyaman;
d. rasa empati;
e. tidak menghakimi;
f. tidak diskriminasi; dan
g. dijamin kerahasiannya.

translated_text:
Article 8
Services for victims of violence are implemented based on the principles of:
a. no fees charged;
b. prompt;
c. safe and comfortable;
d. empathy;
e. non-judgmental;
f. non-discriminatory; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 9
Jenis pelayanan terhadap korban kekerasan meliputi :
a. pelayanan pengaduan dan konsultasi;
b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan bantuan hukum;
d. pelayanan kesehatan;
e. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
f. pelayanan pemulangan; dan
g. pelayanan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 9
Types of services for victims of violence include:
a. complaint and consultation services;
b. assistance services;
c. legal aid services;
d. health services;
e. social rehabilitation services;
f. repatriation services; and
g. social reintegration services.

text:
Pasal 13
(1) Pelayanan Pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf b, dilakukan dalam setiap jenis pelayanan kesehatan, rehabilitasi, bantuan  hukum, reintegrasi sosial, dan pemulangan.
(2) Pendampingan dilakukan oleh tenaga ahli yang mempunyai keahlian  melakukan konseling, terapi dan/atau advokasi untuk penguatan dan  pemulihan perempuan korban kekerasan.
(3) Tenaga ahli yang melakukan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (2) bekerjasama dengan UPTD PPA.
(4) Tenaga ahli sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) wajib disediakan oleh  Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi perempuan.
(5) Tenaga ahli sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) terdiri dari : a. tenaga kesehatan;
b. advokat;
c. pekerja sosial;
d. pembimbing rohani; dan
e. psikolog atau psikiater.

translated_text:
Article 13
(1) Assistance Services as referred to in Article 9 letter b, are carried out in every type of health service, rehabilitation, legal aid, social reintegration, and repatriation.
(2) Assistance is carried out by expert personnel who have expertise in conducting counseling, therapy and/or advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of women victims of violence.
(3) Expert personnel who provide assistance as referred to in paragraph (2) cooperate with UPTD PPA.
(4) Expert personnel as referred to in paragraph (2) must be provided by the Regional Apparatus responsible for women's affairs.
(5) Expert personnel as referred to in paragraph (2) consist of: a. health workers;
b. advocates;
c. social workers;
d. spiritual counselors; and
e. psychologists or psychiatrists.

text:
BAB V
KERJASAMA
Pasal 21
(1) Dalam rangka mencapai tujuan perlindungan perempuan dari tindak  kekerasan Pemerintah Daerah dapat bekerja sama dengan : a. Kementerian;
b. Pemerintah Daerah Provinsi;
c. Pemerintah Daerah Kabupaten/kota;
d. Perguruan tinggi; dan
e. Lembaga non pemerintah.
(2) Kerja sama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi : a. pertukaran data dan informasi;
b. rehabilitasi korban tindak kekerasan;
c. pemulangan dan reintegritasi sosial; dan
d. penyediaan barang bukti dan saksi.

translated_text:
CHAPTER V
COOPERATION
Article 21
(1) In order to achieve the objective of protecting women from acts of violence, the Regional Government may cooperate with:
a. Ministries;
b. Provincial Regional Government;
c. Regency/Municipal Regional Government;
d. Higher education institutions; and
e. Non-governmental institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses.
